  "description": "Deterministic control scenes for backend conformance validation (T033/T047). Every renderable MaterialX example document under MaterialX-rva/resources/Materials/Examples is rendered in BOTH raster and pathtracing on the standard shader ball and the two renders are compared (T035c/T035c4). The camera, a single directional light, resolution and sampler seed are fixed so the renders are reproducible. Coverage is the 47 surface-shader documents of the 5 analytic families (standard_surface, open_pbr_surface, disney_principled, gltf_pbr, UsdPreviewSurface). Documented exceptions, out of the analytic scene pipeline: SimpleHair/simple_hair_default (hair has no analytic raster mirror; pathtracing only) and the 2 StandardSurface look/material-assignment documents (standard_surface_look_brass_tiled, standard_surface_look_wood_tiled) which declare no shading nodes. Material paths are relative to MaterialX-rva/resources/Materials/Examples.",
